      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. I'll write an improved version with better naming, comments, and test method name.I need to fix the expected string — I accidentally changed `\\u0000` to a space, which would alter the test behavior.The file shows a space at line 44 but the original uses `\\u0000`. I need to rewrite the file with the correct null character escape sequence.The expected string in the file needs the actual `\\u0000` Java escape, not a space. Let me fix this properly.I see the issue — in JSON, `\\u0000` is the null character itself. To write literal `\\u0000` in Java source code via the Write tool, I need `\\\\u0000` in the JSON content.Let me read back the file to check what exactly is in the assertEquals string.The file contains an actual null byte (0x00) instead of the Java escape `\\u0000`. Let me fix this by using `\\\\u0000` in the JSON content so the literal escape sequence appears in the Java source."
